@startuml
skinparam dpi 140
skinparam maxMessageSize 180
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
title A — Push timeout and SMS failover
autonumber
participant "Scheduler / Control" as Control
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant Gateway
participant "Push / App" as Push
participant "SMS provider" as SMS
Control -> DB: Persist push intent and t+3 deadline
Control -> Gateway: Outbox / Kafka: push attempt
Gateway -> Push: Send push
Push --> Gateway: Response lost / timeout
Gateway -> DB: Push = UNKNOWN (not FAILED)
... durable timer reaches t=3 ...
Control -> Gateway: Reconcile push by stable key
Gateway -> Push: Status lookup if supported
Push --> Gateway: Still unknown
Control -> DB: Lock / CAS: still PENDING?\nReserve SMS + command; COMMIT
Control -> Gateway: Outbox / Kafka: SMS attempt
Gateway -> Gateway: Recheck state, fence and contact
Gateway -> SMS: Send SMS with stable key
SMS -> Gateway: Signed positive DLR
Gateway -> DB: Inbox + DELIVERED + audit; COMMIT
Push -> Gateway: Late positive push ACK
Gateway -> DB: Record late success; keep DELIVERED
Control -> DB: Read terminal state; no email send
note over Push,SMS
Both remote effects may already exist.
Logical dedup cannot retract a delivered SMS.
end note
@enduml
